From 656f8d54860e5b6bd8eab7e9c3246b0c3f34cb4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:20:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): kanban_create accepts max_retries [daveey]

Workers had no supported way to set a card's retry breaker: kanban_create had
no max_retries and the worker shell is fenced from 'hermes kanban edit'.
kanban_create now takes max_retries (int 1-10, bools refused, omitted = NULL),
validated before placement, and passes it to kb.create_task. hermes-hub
create-task cannot carry it, so a card using it stays local on auto placement
and an explicit pin to another gateway is refused (placement_unavailable)
instead of silently dropping the breaker. The validator lives in the new
tools/kanban_tools_create_args.py (with CREATED_FIELDS moved there) to keep
the kanban_tools facade under its size cap.
